{"title":"2026 CEMC CTMC Problems/Team Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Team_Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bde7059c6b5b207061a12fbd17380fbdff0ea6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> be the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. There is exactly one positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/c/d1c37ef71e8b271d82ff7fe1b57bc248e7b699a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 11 \\times S_{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Team_Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that the sum of the digits of a one-digit number is always equal to that number. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be single digit because it cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times the sum of its digits if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is positive.\n</p><p>Next, let's say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is a two-digit number, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a5153e77dc6c648135060be359b925deaabfa11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 10A + B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/2/a92209a259df0c71b9858258b437dd9c5cb7e8a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5bf77c6740d00af2866f26718d628a60c667ef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, so:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f5bb00c2ceac13554cbea1ebea8b066335976ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10A + B = 11(A + B) = 11A + 11B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"289\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/d/34d5d24b43df3968462d5a7ea4151dbcab302d2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B - 11B = 11A - A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"164\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/5/eb591ca56e36d42cff388b461160b9b5997c4265.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-10B = A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> must be positive and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so this isn't possible.\n</p><p>Next, let's say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is a three-digit number, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/44883176bc140349a258b0422ad246d57cc312a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 100X + 10Y + Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"169\" height=\"16\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/754f1d1f3e44145463158b7ab36f571db03aae0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/957e67f1b088f2ef354e0de05afce3c6108405b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X + Y + Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" />, so:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/6/b36d8642b508011f79a1a244aaefa1155a233691.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100X + 10Y + Z = 11(X + Y + Z) = 11X + 11Y + 11Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"450\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/a/43a11e87b64611befe7e43221f1a0a982acea7ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100X - 11X = 11Y - 10Y + 11Z - Z = Y + 10Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"398\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/d/8ddef59cc79aee4a1b26d342f2e297898a2a0ce0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$89X = Y + 10Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"129\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/a/b9ae647a7bdc7cac62bf005548031f5bc3efffb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/8/5b87257188d43ca8d3ac72fb13c992a3ec55ca1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$89 = Y + 10Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"16\" />, which we realize would work if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/4/404fecd9c732bc2c7596f61b1a84630170322656.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/3/313c4b7c086f78494ed7afafd12ff89bac71a6ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/8/3e85ef86934eb708ad95320119520e02fff0ca21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{198}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Team_Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> multiplied by some integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>The sum of the digits of a number is always congruent to that number mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/c/d1c37ef71e8b271d82ff7fe1b57bc248e7b699a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 11 \\times S_{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/7/9e7339a3a92dc9461560f2520b0ba7c554f980f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 2 \\times c \\pmod{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <i>not</i> equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> must be equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is divisible by both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, meaning that it must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a313bf06349648df7be807bee95b651604ce7a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. THis means that we can try the different multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a313bf06349648df7be807bee95b651604ce7a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to see if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/c/d1c37ef71e8b271d82ff7fe1b57bc248e7b699a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 11 \\times S_{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" /> is true.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/7/8a7124161cc6495f85548ba4de77890ea7241432.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/8/6a8bceb94cdbc297e845959bdc5887473e722518.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{c} = 9 + 9 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/1/511aa2d00210b55efdbfc99830150796fb2009ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 \\times S_{c} = 11 \\times 18 = 198$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"17\" />. This doesn't work out, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a313bf06349648df7be807bee95b651604ce7a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/a/8aad995a0db3f7fb277217cd624e73c85db07475.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 99 \\times 2 = 198$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"135\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/4/bc48173b8f827491880877d2bc893f66dc9b021f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{c} = 1 + 9 + 8 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"17\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0ca20cdc2bbe34d4b6e03012df07d72185f6246.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 \\times S_{c} = 198$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"17\" /> from this, which works out because this is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/c/19c99faf51963acc950fbc05c31700de19c3c25b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{c = 198}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"73\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_CTMC\" title=\"2026 CEMC CTMC\">2026 CEMC CTMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_CTMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 CEMC CTMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_CTMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 CEMC CTMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Prece